course: dictionary
lesson: 8421
title: Rust: a word with three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one. «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster.» Here rust is a verb. It means to become covered in the reddish-brown, flaky coating that forms on iron when it gets wet and meets air.
explain: Look for clues. «Mars looks red because its dust contains iron oxide» describes a colour, so rust here is the reddish-brown colour. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Rust can also be a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some rust, not two rusts. Rust is not a sign of something wearing away by itself. It forms when iron meets water and air, which is why paint and oil help to stop it.
fact: Rust is a reddish-brown, flaky coating that forms on iron or steel when it gets wet and meets air.
fact: Rust can be a noun, a verb or a colour: «The gate was covered in rust», «The old gate began to rust», and «rusty» means covered in rust.
fact: Rust is a chemical change: iron reacts with oxygen and water, so it is a change you cannot undo.
fact: «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster», which is why railings by the sea rust quickly.
fact: Capital R Rust is also the name of a computer language. That is a different meaning from this word.
exercise: «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster.» In this sentence, what does rust mean? | To get very hot | To shine brightly in the sun | To be painted blue | *To become covered in a reddish-brown, flaky coating
exercise: «Mars looks red because its dust contains iron oxide, the same kind of substance as rust.» What colour is rust? | Bright green | *Reddish-brown | Silver | Purple
exercise: Maya says, «My old bike is rusty.» What does rusty mean? | Very fast | Brand new and shiny | *Covered in rust | Made of plastic
test:
Why do people paint metal gates? | *To stop them rusting | To make them heavier | To help them float on water | To turn them into gold
Rust is a chemical change: iron reacts with oxygen and water. What kind of change is it? | A change that is easy to reverse | *A change you cannot undo | A change that only happens in summer | A change that makes iron lighter
exam: In «The old gate began to rust in the rain», which word is a verb? | old | gate | *rust | the
